                <pb facs="0539" n="449" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg449"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/3298</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-11-28T12:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 28,
                                1918, 12 noon</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            November 29, 7.17 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2422. Referring to the Department’s circular telegram of November 16, 6 p.m., and
                    my telegram 2389.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d546-f1"/> I have received from the
                    Minister of Foreign Affairs a note stating that Italian Government agrees in
                    principle with our point of view and is ready to support [our representations],
                    and has so telegraphed to Italian Ambassador at Tokyo.</p>
                <p>Paris informed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson Page</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
